---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy – ispdf';
const description =
  'How ispdf handles your visit and your PDF. Files are resized in your browser and are not uploaded to our server.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <main id="main" class="copy legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-meta">Effective date: 21 October 2026</p>
    <p>
      This policy explains what happens when you use ispdf at <a href="https://ispdf.org/">ispdf.org</a>. It matches how
      the site works today: the resize tool runs in your browser, and we do not ask you to create an account.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      The site is operated as ispdf. For privacy questions, email
      <a href="mailto:contact@ispdf.org">contact@ispdf.org</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your PDF</h2>
    <p>
      When you resize a PDF, the file is read and processed on your device. The document is not uploaded to an ispdf
      server, and we do not receive its contents, file name, or the text inside it. The resized file is created in your
      browser for you to download. Closing or reloading the page clears that working copy from the page.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because the file stays on your device, we cannot recover it for you later, and we do not use PDF contents to train
      models or for advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>Information from a normal visit</h2>
    <p>
      Loading the website still contacts the host that serves ispdf.org. Like most sites, that host may record standard
      connection data needed to deliver the pages and to limit abuse. That can include your IP address, the date and
      time, the browser type, and the address of the page you requested, such as the homepage or this policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      Those logs are about the web request. They do not include the PDF you select in the tool. ispdf does not use them
      to build a marketing profile. We do not control the host’s exact retention period. The host keeps logs for its
      ordinary security and operations needs.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and site measurement</h2>
    <p>
      ispdf uses Google Analytics to see how the site is used, such as which pages are opened. The measurement tag is
      loaded from Google and uses the ID G-9H5YSQ5R26. It can set cookies in your browser, including cookies named
      _ga, and it sends Google technical details of the visit: the page address, the time, browser and device
      information, the referring page, and your IP address. Google uses that information as described in
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a>. You can also install
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google’s Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      We also use Plausible Analytics, loaded from plausible.io. Plausible does not set cookies. It counts page views
      and records the page address, the referring page, the browser, the device, and a general location. Plausible
      describes this in <a href="https://plausible.io/privacy">its privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Neither analytics tool receives your PDF, its file name, or the text inside it. We do not use advertising
      cookies, and the resize tool does not use cookies to remember your file. We do not run a sign-in system.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
    <p>
      We do not ask for your name, email address, or payment details to use the resize tool. We do not sell personal
      information. We do not receive the contents of your PDF, so we cannot share those contents with anyone else.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have the right to ask what personal information we hold, to correct it, to
      delete it, or to object to certain uses, and you may be able to complain to a data-protection authority. The
      information described above is ordinary hosting logs and the visit data Google Analytics and Plausible receive.
      Email
      <a href="mailto:contact@ispdf.org">contact@ispdf.org</a> and we will respond.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      ispdf is a general document tool. It is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect personal
      information from them.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page with a new effective date. Continued use
      of the site after that date means the new policy applies to later visits.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
